WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:06.253
Measure in cost per completed task, with failures and retries in the numerator.

3
00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:13.595
Know which of the six buckets your tokens land in, and remember that history grows roughly with the square of the turn count.

4
00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:20.424
Price from the usage fields, add the three input meters to get prompt size, and reconcile against the provider.

5
00:00:20.704 --> 00:00:22.859
Layer your budgets and alert on rates.

6
00:00:23.139 --> 00:00:26.808
When you present the numbers, show the distribution and the assumptions.

7
00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:31.184
The next lesson pulls the biggest levers: caching, batching, and routing.
